# ERP Entity Document Browser Standard

## Phase

HR.DOC_BROWSER.1 — Employee Document Browser (2026-08-03).
Reference implementation: `/admin/hr/document-browser` (employees + dependents).

This design MUST be reused when building document browsers for other entities:
equipment, customers, vendors, vehicles, projects, etc.

---

## The Pattern — 3 Resizable Columns

```
┌───────────────┬──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┐
│ Column 1      │ Column 2             │ Column 3                     │
│ NAVIGATOR     │ DOCUMENT LIST        │ PREVIEW                      │
│ (entity tree) │ (docs for selection) │ (inline file + metadata)     │
│ resizable     │ resizable            │ flex-1 (takes the rest)      │
└───────────────┴──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┘
```

- Shell: `flex h-[calc(100vh-190px)] min-h-[480px] rounded-lg border overflow-hidden`
- Columns 1 and 2 have fixed pixel widths held in React state; Column 3 is `flex-1 min-w-0`
- Between columns: a draggable resize handle (`role="separator"`, `cursor-col-resize`)
- Column widths persist to `localStorage` under a versioned key
  (e.g. `hr-doc-browser-col-widths-v1`), clamped to min/max on restore

### Canonical files (copy this structure per module)

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/server/actions/hr/doc-browser.ts` | `get{X}DocBrowserEmployees` (tree) + `get{X}DocBrowserDocuments` (docs per entity) |
| `src/features/hr/document-browser/hr-doc-browser-page-client.tsx` | Shell: selection state, resize logic, document fetch via `useTransition` |
| `src/features/hr/document-browser/hr-doc-browser-navigator.tsx` | Column 1: search + status filter + expandable tree |
| `src/features/hr/document-browser/hr-doc-browser-doc-list.tsx` | Column 2: document rows with type/status/expiry badges |
| `src/features/hr/document-browser/hr-doc-browser-preview.tsx` | Column 3: metadata strip + file tabs + inline preview |
| `src/features/hr/document-browser/hr-doc-browser-resize-handle.tsx` | Draggable divider |
| `src/features/hr/document-browser/hr-doc-browser-types.ts` | `BrowserEntitySelection` shared client type |
| `src/app/(protected)/admin/hr/document-browser/page.tsx` | SSR shell: auth + initial navigator data |

For a new module, replace `hr`/employee terminology with the target entity and keep
the same file layout under `src/features/<module>/document-browser/`.

---

## Rule 1 — DMS is the single source of documents

The document list MUST come from `dms_document_links` filtered by
`entity_type` + `entity_id` (entity types from `src/lib/dms/dms-entity-types.ts`).
Never create per-module document tables. Module-native records that reference a
DMS document (like `employee_identity_documents.dms_document_id`) may be merged
into the list as extra sources with a distinct `source` label, deduplicated by
DMS document id.

## Rule 2 — Unified document row shape

Server actions return a flat, UI-ready row:

```ts
export type HrDocBrowserDocument = {
  id: number | null;              // dms_documents.id — null for metadata-only rows
  documentNo: string | null;
  title: string;
  typeNameEn: string | null;
  status: string | null;
  issueDate: string | null;
  expiryDate: string | null;
  source: "dms_link" | "hr_identity" | "dependent_link";  // extend per module
  files: { id: number; fileName: string; mimeType: string | null; fileSizeBytes: number | null }[];
};
```

Rows are sorted expiry-ascending (nulls last) so urgent documents surface first.

## Rule 3 — Preview via the /api/dms/file proxy ONLY

- Inline preview: `/api/dms/file?fileId={id}&disposition=inline`
  - `application/pdf` → `<iframe>`
  - `image/*` → `<img>`
  - anything else → download card (no inline preview)
- Download: `/api/dms/file?fileId={id}&disposition=attachment` via a plain `<a href>`
- NEVER call Supabase storage or signed URLs directly from browser components.

## Rule 4 — Navigator behavior

- Search box filters the tree client-side (name/code, including child names).
- Status filter chips: All / Active / Inactive. Inactive entities stay VISIBLE
  but greyed out (`opacity-60`) with an "Inactive" badge — do not hide them.
- Child entities (dependents, sub-assets…) expand inline via a chevron that is a
  separate click target from row selection.
- Selection state lives in the page client as
  `{ type, id, name, subtitle }` (`BrowserEntitySelection`).

## Rule 5 — Data loading contract

- Column 1 data is loaded server-side in `page.tsx` and passed as a prop.
- Column 2 loads on selection via a server action inside `useTransition`
  (spinner while pending, toast on error).
- Selecting an entity auto-selects the first document so the preview is never
  pointlessly empty.
- Document selection is index-based (rows with `id: null` exist).

## Rule 6 — Open Full Record opens a workspace tab

DMS-backed rows (`id != null`) get an "Open Full Record" button calling
`openTab({ route: "/dms/documents/record/{id}", tabKind: "record", entityType: "dms_document", entityId: id, closable: true })`.
Metadata-only rows must not render the button.

## Rule 7 — Page + registration requirements

Every new browser MUST:
1. Guard the page server-side: module view permission AND `dms.documents.view`
   (or `dms.admin` / `system_admin`), redirecting to `/access-denied`.
2. Re-check the same permissions inside every server action.
3. Register the route in `src/lib/workspace/workspace-route-registry.ts`
   (`tabKind: "list"`, `singleton: true`).
4. Add a sidebar entry under the owning module (NOT under DMS).

## Rule 8 — Resize handle contract (D5)

- `mousedown` on the handle starts a drag tracked with document-level
  `mousemove`/`mouseup` listeners; set `body { user-select: none; cursor: col-resize }`
  during the drag and remove on release.
- Clamp: navigator 200–420px, list 260–560px (adjust per module if justified).
- Persist widths to `localStorage` on mouseup only (not per pixel).

## Forbidden patterns

```tsx
// ❌ NEVER — module-specific document tables
supabase.from("equipment_documents")...

// ❌ NEVER — direct storage access from the browser UI
supabase.storage.from("dms-documents").createSignedUrl(...)

// ❌ NEVER — hiding inactive entities instead of greying them out
employees.filter((e) => e.status === "active")   // without a user-facing filter

// ❌ NEVER — CSS-only resize (no persistence, breaks min/max)
<div className="resize-x overflow-auto">
```
